# Application Layer Patterns

## Services

- Inject repository interfaces directly (no Unit of Work)
- `userId` always passed as method parameter from controller — set on entities in service, never from DTO
- One `SaveChangesAsync()` per operation (implicit EF transaction)
- Use AutoMapper for entity ↔ DTO mapping (`Mappings/MappingProfile.cs`)

```csharp
if (expense.UserId != userId)
    throw new UnauthorizedException("You do not have permission...");
```

## DTOs & Validators

- DTOs in `DTOs/` — one file per DTO, suffix `Dto` (e.g. `CreateExpenseDto`)
- Validators in `Validators/` using FluentValidation `AbstractValidator<T>`
- Register validators via `AddValidatorsFromAssembly` in `DependencyInjection.cs`
- Query param DTOs (e.g. `ExpenseFilterDto`) need manual validation trigger

## Interfaces

- Service interfaces in `Interfaces/` (e.g. `IExpenseService`)
- Repository interfaces in `Repositories/` (e.g. `IExpenseRepository`)
- IO-bound implementations (JWT, CSV, password hash) → interface in Application, impl in Infrastructure

## Response DTO Safety

- Never expose `PasswordHash`, internal IDs of other users, or `UserEmail` on expenses
- `IsPredefined` never trusted from client input
- Update `API_DOC.md` when DTO shapes change (frontend is a separate repo)
